  "source": "# The art of noticing\n\nA quiet page, a little time, and a word that stays with you.\n\n## Along the river\n\n🙂 café café 東京. We walked along the {{bank||bank||The land beside a river.||From Old Norse bakki.||embankment}}. Later, we passed the {{bank||bank||A place that keeps and lends money.||From Italian banca, a bench.||banker}}.\n\nReading slowly makes room for **small discoveries**, *new connections*, and &&ordinary wonders&&. Keep the original punctuation: 你好，世界！\n\n> “Attention is the beginning of understanding.”\n\n- Select a word or phrase and choose Define.\n- Tap a marked word to see its embedded meaning.\n- Make room for the final sentence.\n\n1. Read a little.\n2. Come back tomorrow.\n\n## 日本語\n\n<ruby>東京<rp>（</rp><rt>とうきょう</rt><rp>）</rp></ruby>で、{{腕組||腕組||抱着胳膊}}をして考える。言葉を一つずつ、ゆっくりと。\n\n## More voices\n\n{{se rendre compte||se rendre compte||意识到}}. {{欢迎||欢迎||Welcome}}！ {{ontdekken||ontdekken||to discover}}.\n\n[Read with Leximory](https://leximory.com). An image keeps its alternative text:\n\n![A quiet forest](https://fixtures.leximory.invalid/forest.png)\n\n:::fixture_recording\n## Listen to this passage\n\nThe recording belongs to this section. The {{leaves||leaf||The flat, green parts of a plant.}} move in the breeze. This text stays visible even when audio is unavailable.\n:::\n\n:::missing_recording\nThis section has no available recording. It still has all of its text.\n:::\n\n## Readable fallbacks\n\n```latex\nE = mc^2\n```\n\nA malformed marker keeps its visible word: {{unfinished||secret metadata. No metadata should become prose.\n\n---\n\n## Final section\n\nThe last sentence matters just as much as the first.\n",
